<<~ ahu #/lab>>

! The Meme API Surface ~ the work QA lab

''Register: Reference.'' One page, every door a meme answers at, read off the live contact rather than off intent. A row without a witness names itself as owed.

''The lab.'' A bare TiddlyWiki server carrying the packed plugin — nothing of the island, nothing of the daemon:

```
pnpm --filter @lararium/tw5 build:plugin
mkdir -p lab/tiddlers && cp packages/lararium-tw5/dist-plugin/lares-memetic-wikitext.tid lab/tiddlers/
echo '{"description":"meme lab","plugins":[],"themes":[]}' > lab/tiddlywiki.info
node TiddlyWiki5/tiddlywiki.js lab --listen port=8080 host=127.0.0.1
```

The same lab stands on a published engine: swap the first argument for `npm pack tiddlywiki@5.4.1`'s `package/tiddlywiki.js`. The plugin drops into stock (#/pristine).

''The container law.'' A 1-wiki server holds ONE container, and `recipes/default` and `bags/default` both name it — `default` names THE HOST'S ANCHOR. Any other recipe or bag answers `404` with a one-line body before the path or the body gets read; a bag the server cannot name swallows nothing.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/paths>>

!! Paths and methods

The meme's URI projects onto the path with the scheme as its own segment: `lar:///ha.ka.ba/x` reads `/bags/default/memes/lar/ha.ka.ba/x` — typable, no percent-encoding. Authority-less URIs alone: a session-form authority IS the HTTP authority and never rides the path.

| method | path | does | answers |
|---|---|---|---|
| `PUT` | `/{recipes\|bags}/default/memes/<scheme>/<path>` | the whole meme arrives as text and lands as its records through the Confluence gate (`placeMeme`) | `200` receipt JSON · `412` · `422` · `400` · `404` |
| `GET` | `/{recipes\|bags}/default/memes/<scheme>/<path>` | the whole meme, children recomposed inline (`readMeme`) | `200` text · `404` · `400` |
| `DELETE` | `/bags/default/memes/<scheme>/<path>` | the group leaves — root · `#/slot` fragments · `/path` children (`removeMeme`). A removal addresses a BAG, as stock's `delete-tiddler.js` does; the `/recipes/` form answers `404` the same way stock's does | `204` · `412` · `404` · `400` |
| `GET` | `/{recipes\|bags}/default/memes.json[?tree=1]` | every ROOT with its canonical hash (`listMemes`); `tree=1` nests each root's slot tree. A sibling of stock's `tiddlers.json`: a `$:/`-titled root rides only while `$:/config/SyncSystemTiddlersFromServer` reads `yes` | `200` JSON array · `404` |
| `PUT` | `/recipes/default/tiddlers/<title>` | THE NATIVE DOOR, gated ahead of stock: a framed root refuses (#/two-doors); every other record reaches stock's own handler | `422` · stock's `204` |

Both container kinds read the same records on a plain server; on an island `--recipe` reads the wiki's whole cascade top-down and writes its designated bag — <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/recipe-layer-model">>.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/headers>>

!! Headers

| header | on | carries |
|---|---|---|
| `ETag: "sha256:<hex>"` | every answer holding a canonical hash (GET · PUT · 412s) | the house's canonical hash of the render the records carry now — the merge base a writer hands back |
| `Repr-Digest: sha-256=:<base64>:` | beside every `ETag` | the same hash in the RFC 9530 field, so a client verifies the body without learning the house's tag grammar; `digestsEqual` reads either spelling |
| `If-Match: "<sha256:hex>"` | PUT · DELETE | the base the writer read; records that moved past it answer `412` and nothing moves. Absent = a fresh adoption (PUT) or an unconditioned removal (DELETE) |
| `If-None-Match: *` | PUT | create-only (RFC 9110 §13.1.2): a URI any record already stands under answers `412` before the gate runs. A tag list reads as no precondition |
| `Content-Type: text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki; charset=utf-8` | GET | the carrier type |
| `Content-Type: application/json` | PUT receipts · 412 bodies · `memes.json` · the native gate's 422 | |
| `x-requested-with: TiddlyWiki` | every non-GET | stock's CSRF gate, unchanged in front of these routes (`csrf-disable` lifts it) |
| `WWW-Authenticate: Basic …` | 401 | stock's principal table, unchanged (#/principals) |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/status>>

!! The status table

| status | meaning | body |
|---|---|---|
| `200` | PUT `ingest` — records landed, stale children tombstoned, `ETag` = the new hash · PUT `noop` — the records already carry this text, `ETag` = the standing hash · GET the meme · `memes.json` the listing | the receipt `{uri, decision, grade, landed, tombstoned, canonicalHash, warnings, diagnostics}` · the text · the array |
| `204` | DELETE removed the group · stock's native door landed a plain record | empty |
| `400` | a malformed path segment (a broken percent-escape) | `malformed meme path` — the SKIN answered, never the server's no-route floor |
| `401` | the principal table refused — anonymous under `readers=(authenticated)`, a reader-only principal writing | stock's, with `WWW-Authenticate` |
| `404` | no root stands under the URI · no such recipe or bag (the one-line body names it) · DELETE under `/recipes/` | empty, or the one line |
| `412` | the records moved past the writer's `If-Match` · a record stands where `If-None-Match: *` asked for none | `{uri, decision: "conflict", reason, canonicalHash}` + the live `ETag` |
| `422` | PUT of a meme grading `error` (a carrier that stopped round-tripping); nothing lands · the native door met a framed root | the receipt with `diagnostics` · `{uri, door, reason}` |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/two-doors>>

!! The two doors

A framed meme root lands whole through the native tiddler door and never splits; the `/memes/` door splits it. Three seams keep the two apart, each measured on the live contact:

# ''The native gate (a).'' `PUT /recipes/default/tiddlers/<title>` with a carrier-typed body that still opens with a SOH head answers `422` and names the door: `{"uri": "lar:///t/native", "door": "/recipes/default/memes/lar/t/native", "reason": "…"}`. Nothing lands. A plain tiddler, a split root (a `<<~ kahea …>>` body, no head), a slot child, and a head shown inside a fence all pass to stock. `bag` IS USER SPACE on this door too: stock's `get-tiddler.js` stamps `bag: "default"` over the JSON it serves, and a stock client hands that stamp back on save — a `bag` naming the anchor reads as the envelope and never lands; any other value reads as the author's and lands as written.
# ''The client charm (b).'' The stock tiddlyweb syncadaptor speaks the native door for every record; the plugin's startup module decorates the live adaptor so a record `framedRootOf` names rides `PUT /recipes/<recipe>/memes/<scheme>/<path>` with the meme text as its body, the route's `ETag` as the revision. A framed root added in the browser arrives on the server split; the plain control arrives through the native door as ever.
# ''The backstop (c).'' A root landed by a door neither the gate nor the charm sees — the engine's own `--load`, `$tw.wiki.importTiddler` — re-stamps on the server, and the log carries ONE line: `[memetic-wikitext] re-stamped <uri> (landed via a native write)`.

''A SLOT CHILD IS A TIDDLER.'' The native door lands it as one, ungated, and the root re-cuts on the server — a child's save never addresses `/memes/`. The root law reads one spelling (`isMemeRoot`): a record of the carrier type, no `#` in its title, no `$fragment-parent`. A child into which an author pasted a whole framed carrier wears every mark a founding wears and is still a child: its frame stands as AUTHORED TEXT, no `uri#/a#/z` is ever minted, and the gate answers `204` rather than `422` — a refusal on a path the stock syncer drives stalls its queue permanently.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/principals>>

!! The principal table ~ parity with `/tiddlers/`

The server's method→principal mapping and its authenticator run before any route gets chosen, so the meme skins inherit the table stock's `/tiddlers/` answers from — measured on stock's own path first, asserted as parity on ours:

| principal | `GET /tiddlers/…` | `GET /memes/…` | `PUT` · `DELETE /memes/…` |
|---|---|---|---|
| anonymous under `readers=(authenticated)` | `401` + `WWW-Authenticate: Basic` | the same status, the same header | `401` |
| a reader (`bob`, off the `writers=` list) | `200` | `200` | `401` — as stock refuses, nothing moves |
| a writer (`alice`) | `200` | `200` | `200` · `204` |

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/pristine>>

!! The pristine claim ~ with its version

''Claim:'' the packed plugin drops into a PUBLISHED TiddlyWiki, not only into the fork.

''Measure:'' `meme-routes.e2e` takes `LARES_TW5_JS` and runs the whole contact — PUT · GET · DELETE · `memes.json` · the native door · the readers/writers case · the `--render` door — against any `tiddlywiki.js`, and writes the engine's version to the stream: `meme-routes.e2e: contact with TiddlyWiki 5.4.1 at …/package/tiddlywiki.js`.

| engine | version | result |
|---|---|---|
| the fork (`TiddlyWiki5/`, tracks `upstream/master`) | `5.5.0-prerelease` | 17/17 |
| `npm pack tiddlywiki@5.4.1` (the published line) | `5.4.1` | 17/17 |

The witness landed at `f144ed242` (14/14 then; the listing added three). Its `put-tiddler.js` / `get-tiddler.js` / `get-tiddlers-json.js` read the same on both lines; the route table sorts by `info.priority` and reads `methods` the same. ''Its invoker:'' the `pristine-upstream` job in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` — pinned to ONE version at the workflow's `TW5_PRISTINE`, cached by that version, failing when the contact line names no engine or another one (a skipped suite reads green to vitest).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/skins>>

!! The four skins ~ verb parity

One law, four skins. Every row calls the same function in `packages/lararium-tw5/src/place-meme.ts`; a skin supplies a sink and nothing more. `base` on a verb, `--base`/`--if-match` on the CLI and `If-Match` on the route spell ONE hash.

| law | route (plain server) | daemon verb | CLI | MCP tool |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `placeMeme` | `PUT …/memes/<scheme>/<path>` | `meme-put {recipe?, bag?, uri, text, base?}` | `lares meme put <uri> [--recipe\|--bag] [--base] [--file]` | `meme_put(uri, text, recipe?, bag?, base?)` |
| `readMeme` | `GET …/memes/<scheme>/<path>` | `meme-get {recipe?, bag?, uri}` | `lares meme get <uri> [--recipe\|--bag]` | `meme_get(uri, recipe?, bag?)` |
| `listMemes` | `GET …/memes.json[?tree=1]` | `meme-list {recipe?, bag?, tree?}` | `lares meme list [--recipe\|--bag] [--tree]` | `meme_list(recipe?, bag?, tree?)` |
| `removeMeme` | `DELETE /bags/…/memes/<scheme>/<path>` | `meme-delete {recipe?, bag?, uri, base?}` | `lares meme delete <uri> [--recipe\|--bag] [--if-match]` | `meme_delete(uri, recipe?, bag?, base?)` |
| the projection | `tiddlywiki --render` through the house templates | `meme-project {recipe?, bag?, uri, to}` | `lares meme project <uri\|file> --to <mem\|md\|html\|tid\|json>` | `meme_project(uri, to, recipe?, bag?)` |
| `normalizeMemeSource` · the check | — (a file law) | — | `lares meme normalize` · `lares meme check [--gradient\|--edges]` | — (LOCAL seat, by law) |

The in-VM face publishes the same verbs to a wiki-side caller as `$tw.lares.meme.{place, read, list, remove, normalize, check, project, recompose, parse}`. The CLI's exit classes: a `conflict` exits `conflict`; an absent meme on `get` or `delete` exits `not-found`; a refusal exits `verb-error`. The fixture `packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts/fixtures/cli-verbs.json` welds the MCP names to the CLI spellings; `tools/mirror-parity-witness.sh` reds when it goes stale. The CLI door law: <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/cli/vessel-door">>.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/walkthrough>>

!! A curl walkthrough

Against the lab on `127.0.0.1:8080`, with `x.mem` a framed carrier declaring `uri-path = "t/x"`:

```
# found it — create-only, so a standing record never gets overwritten
curl -si -X PUT -H 'x-requested-with: TiddlyWiki' -H 'If-None-Match: *' \
  --data-binary @x.mem http://127.0.0.1:8080/bags/default/memes/lar/t/x
#   HTTP/1.1 200 · ETag: "sha256:…" · Repr-Digest: sha-256=:…: · {"decision":"ingest",…}

# read it back; keep the ETag as the base
curl -si http://127.0.0.1:8080/recipes/default/memes/lar/t/x
#   HTTP/1.1 200 · Content-Type: text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki · the whole meme, children inline

# list the roots; nest the slots
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8080/recipes/default/memes.json
#   [{"uri":"lar:///t/x","canonicalHash":"sha256:…"}]
curl -s 'http://127.0.0.1:8080/recipes/default/memes.json?tree=1'
#   [{"uri":"lar:///t/x","canonicalHash":"sha256:…","slots":[{"slot":"#/a","uri":"lar:///t/x#/a","slots":[]}]}]

# edit against the base you read — a stale base answers 412 and lands nothing
curl -si -X PUT -H 'x-requested-with: TiddlyWiki' -H 'If-Match: "sha256:…"' \
  --data-binary @x.mem http://127.0.0.1:8080/bags/default/memes/lar/t/x

# the native door refuses a framed root and names the door
curl -si -X PUT -H 'x-requested-with: TiddlyWiki' \
  -d '{"title":"lar:///t/y","type":"text/memetic-wikitext+tiddlywiki","text":"<<^ code=\"&#x0001;\" …>>…"}' \
  http://127.0.0.1:8080/recipes/default/tiddlers/lar%3A%2F%2F%2Ft%2Fy
#   HTTP/1.1 422 · {"uri":"lar:///t/y","door":"/recipes/default/memes/lar/t/y","reason":"…"}

# a container the server cannot name swallows nothing
curl -si -X PUT -H 'x-requested-with: TiddlyWiki' --data-binary @x.mem http://127.0.0.1:8080/bags/other/memes/lar/t/x
#   HTTP/1.1 404 · no such bag: other (this server names only default)

# remove the group — a bag address, conditioned on the base
curl -si -X DELETE -H 'x-requested-with: TiddlyWiki' -H 'If-Match: "sha256:…"' http://127.0.0.1:8080/bags/default/memes/lar/t/x
#   HTTP/1.1 204 · a stale If-Match: 412 and the group stands · /recipes/…: 404
```

The same walk through the other skins: `lares meme put lar:///t/x --file x.mem` · `lares meme get lar:///t/x` · `lares meme list --tree` · `lares meme delete lar:///t/x --if-match sha256:…`; over MCP, `meme_put` · `meme_get` · `meme_list(tree=True)` · `meme_delete(base=…)`.

<<~/ahu>>

